A constant template is finished during compilation.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    title #= "Moth"

    heading #= [$md:
        # [title]
    ]
]

A direct top-level const template needs an explicit root purpose in the accepted
queued design. `$page` is the first HTML purpose but is not implemented yet; the
Alpha compiler still uses activity-based entry selection and reserved `page_*`
metadata.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    #[$md:
        # Compile-time heading
    ]
]

Assigned or returned templates remain ordinary values, not direct page fragments.

Const template loops have an iteration limit so an accidental build-time loop
cannot run forever.
